+# Todo Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Optional editable calendar due dates, UTC overdue filtering in API and list.
+
+**Architecture:** Extend the existing immutable Todo records and singleton store. Use nullable DateOnly and a presence-aware PATCH property, a TimeProvider for UTC dates, and simple Blazor forms calling the store directly.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor interactive server, System.Text.Json, xUnit, existing WebApplicationFactory and Playwright MCP.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-todo-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Keine neuen NuGet-Pakete.
+- TDD: zuerst ein fehlschlagender Test unter `tests/`.
+- Neue für Tests verwendete UI-Elemente erhalten `data-testid`.
+- Kein Sortieren, keine Erinnerungen oder Styling-Änderungen.
+- Überfällig: nicht erledigt und Datum vor dem heutigen UTC-Kalendertag.
+- Draft-PR gegen `main`; kein Merge und kein Schließen des Tickets.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Omitted PATCH date preserves the value, explicit null clears it, including alongside a done/title change.
+- UTC midnight changes overdue status; local date and equality to today must not change the rule.
+- Invalid dates, timestamps, non-string JSON dates and impossible leap days return HTTP 400 with an error object and leave stored data intact.
+- A filtered list excludes done/undated/today/future todos and includes a past-due todo once reopened.
+- Clearing a browser date and saving must remove it; toggling the filter and blank-title validation must leave the page usable.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store dates and central UTC overdue rule
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`; test `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- `Todo(int Id, string Title, bool Done, DateOnly? DueDate = null)` with `bool IsOverdue(DateOnly todayUtc)`.
+- `NewTodo(string? Title, DateOnly? DueDate = null)`.
+- Preserve `TodoPatch(string? Title, bool? Done)`; add `DateOnly? DueDate { get; init; }` whose setter records presence, plus a JSON-ignored read-only presence indicator `HasDueDate`.
+- `TodoStore(TimeProvider? timeProvider = null)` defaults to `TimeProvider.System`.
+- `IReadOnlyList<Todo> List(bool? overdue = null)` and `bool IsOverdue(Todo todo)` use UTC day from that provider; existing Add/Update/Get signatures remain.
+
